{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["The reason for specifying <b>And a man or a woman</b> is on account of 'the zaqan [beard],' and furthermore because he needs to say concerning 'the bald spot and the forehead-baldness,' 'a man' and not 'a person,' so as to exclude the woman. Now the interpretation (interp. by M[?].H[?], 'And a man or a woman,' meaning: since he used the word 'a man,' which does not include a woman as does the word 'a person,' he needed to say 'a woman' on account of the head, not on account of the zaqan, for the zaqan applies to a man and not to a woman. And concerning the bald spot and the forehead-baldness he said, as he said, 'And a man when his head becomes bare,' and did not mention in it 'a woman,' because baldness and forehead-baldness are not found in a woman because of the moisture that is in her, as he explains below. And what he said, 'and not a person,' means: and he did not say 'a person,' which is a collective term for man and woman — end of quotation) [is] when there is a lesion in it, on the head or on the zaqan of a man."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The parenthetical (פי׳ מ״ח ... עד כאן) is a quotation from an unnamed commentator; the abbreviation מ״ח is unresolved and may stand for a proper name or epithet. The final phrase כי יהיה בו נגע בראש או בזקן לאיש appears to be Ibn Ezra resuming his own voice, quoting the verse's conclusion."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:55.936048205Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}